{
  "id": 438706450,
  "iid": 22675,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "proto: Fix proto_registrar_dump_fieldcount() to skip index 0",
  "description": "This fixes a bug in proto_registrar_dump_fieldcount() where\nindex 0 is not being ignored when calling `tshark -G fieldcount`\nand is being erroneously reported both as an extra registered field\ncount and extra deregistered field.\n\nWhile here refactor the dump field count function to use a programatic API\nthat is more generic and widely useful. Add a new public\nfunction that returns several counts and use that instead.\n\nAlso fix other dump functions to ignore invalid index 0,\nalthough those functions weren't giving incorrect results\nbecause they already skip NULL values.\n\nFixup 7d0b92aa0e3d91ce899107b8a94ca1edcf251134.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-12-08T01:06:31.645Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-12-08T15:47:05.513Z",
